# ASP.NET Core and EF Core

- Controllers and minimal APIs validate input and return one error shape (Problem Details when the app already uses it).
- Authorization is policy-based and applied on the endpoint, not only in the UI.
- EF queries that are read many times are async (`ToListAsync`, `SaveChangesAsync`) and do not query inside a loop.
- Migrations ship with the change that needs them. Secrets stay out of `appsettings` that is committed.
